<!-- HERO -->
<header class="post-hero">
  <div class="tags">
    <span class="tag tag-purple">Long Context</span>
    <span class="tag tag-cyan">KV Cache</span>
    <span class="tag tag-green">Interactive</span>
  </div>
  <h1>FlashMemory: 86% Less KV Cache, Same Accuracy</h1>
  <p class="lead">LLMs drag the entire conversation history into GPU memory even when generating a reply that needs only the last 8 K tokens — a colossal waste. FlashMemory-DeepSeek-V4 fixes this with <em>Lookahead Sparse Attention</em>: a tiny retrieval indexer that, every 64 decoding steps, predicts exactly which historical chunks the next window will need and pages them in from CPU. The result is an 86.5% reduction in KV cache memory — down to 13.5% of baseline — with a +0.6% accuracy gain.</p>
  <div class="post-hero-meta">
    <span>June 10, 2026</span>
    <span>~11 min read</span>
    <span>Paper: <code>arXiv:2606.09079</code></span>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-links">
    <a class="hero-btn" href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.09079" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
